## Rules
1. Keep ALL facts accurate. Never invent experience, companies, dates, or skills.
2. Extract the top keywords/skills from the job description and weave them in where truthful.
3. Rewrite the summary to address this specific role and company (3–4 sentences).
4. Bullets: PRESERVE ALL original bullets — never reduce the bullet count per role. You may rephrase a bullet to better match the job, but do not drop any. For the most recent role, expand to 5–6 bullets if possible. Older roles keep all original bullets.
5. Surface the most relevant skills first.
